\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Reference databases change often, but usually only in part.} (a) Pfam grew from 21{,}979 to 30{,}134 families over eight releases; blue segments show the net families each release added. (b) Comparing every model of Pfam 38.2 with 38.1, ignoring build\nobreakdash -date, build\nobreakdash -command, and comment lines: 86.6\% are identical. Only 13.4\% (new or edited) can produce new results, yet a conventional update recomputes 100\%. Blue marks what TARE\xspace  reruns. Panel (b) is the pair we time; \cref  {fig:pairs} measures the six neighboring releases the same way (median changed fraction 12.2\%).}}{2}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
